e><surname>Frank</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Galgan</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Petersson</surname><given-names>LR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Secondary copper deficiency, chromium deficiency and trace element imbalance in the moose (<italic>Alces alces </italic>L.) Effect of anthropogenic activity</article-title><source>Ambio</source><year>1994</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>315</fpage><lpage>317</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gooneratne</surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name><name><surname>Buckley</surname><given-names>WT</given-names></name><name><surname>Christensen</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Review of copper deficiency and metabolism in ruminants</article-title><source>Can J Anim Sci</source><year>1989</year><volume>69</volume><fpage>819</fpage><lpage>845</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hainline</surname><given-names>BE</given-names></name><name><surname>Rajagopalan</surname><given-names>KV</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Rose J</surname></name></person-group><source>Molybdenum in animal and human health. in: Trace elements in health, a review of current sites</source><year>1983</year><publisher-name>London Butterworth</publisher-name><fpage>150</fpage><lpage>166</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Harris</surname><given-names>ED</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The iron &#x02013; copper connection: The link to ceruloplasmin grows stronger</article-title><source>Nutr Rev</source><year>1995</year><volume>53</volume><fpage>170</fpage><lpage>173</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmi